# File: tests/features/add_greeting_non_ascii_count_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/377-add-greeting-non-ascii-count-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Count non-ASCII characters in the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Count non-ASCII characters in a plain greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_non_ascii_count is called with Ada, Zo U+00EB, and U+674E U+96F7
    Then the results are 0, then 1, then 2
    And each result is an int

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Count code points without normalization
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_non_ascii_count is called with Zoe U+0308 and Ada space U+1F600
    Then the results are 1, then 1
    And each result equals the number of code points above 127 in greet of the same name

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_non_ascii_count is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_non_ascii_count of Zo U+00EB
    Then it prints 1 and greeting_non_ascii_count is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the code-point counting rule and the inherited invalid-name error
